# Fix-chain rules

Read the complete original brief at .t3/inputs/inputs/fix/brief/prompt.md and every file under .t3/inputs/inputs/fix/brief/inputs/. Read context under .t3/inputs/inputs/fix/context/. Keep the original scope, acceptance criteria and base constraints. Tests named in the original brief must still exist and pass; removal or weakening is a regression.

After checking out the exact dependency commit and before writing reports or editing source, run `{{.ReportPathCheck}}`. On failure, stop with the specific report-path collision; do not delete tracked files, change classification, or add ignore rules. These output-only paths supersede report locations in the original brief. Never create or modify root continuation.md or handoff.md.

Create artifacts/continuation.md immediately and keep its goal, checklist, current step, blockers and last verification current. Only declared artifacts are retained. List .t3/dependencies/ to discover producer directories; never hard-code dependency namespaces. Read commit provenance records and check out the exact dependency commit before work; never invent a moving branch or base.

Fixers: address only the blocking findings listed in the source review and stay within the original brief. Change nothing for notes. Reproduce each listed blocking finding with a failing regression test before implementation, run focused checks, and record verification commands and exit codes. Record anything else in a FOLLOW-UPS section of artifacts/handoff.md. If a listed finding cannot be fixed within the original brief, stop and report rather than redesign. Perform the test-integrity check by listing removed existing test lines with git diff <original-base> -- '*_test.go'; justify every removal or change and never weaken an assertion to pass. While iterating, run `make test-affected BASE=<original-base>` where the repository has that make target, using the pinned base recorded in the original brief, not the preceding fix commit; with Huyang, use `verify_run` with `test_scope=affected`. Otherwise run focused checks of the changed packages and their importers. The worker runs the declared final gate once outside the agent turn; do not run a separate full agent gate. Only source, regression tests and intended product documentation enter the declared fix commit. Reports are output-only: keep all declared artifacts/ reports untracked, retain them through declared outputs, and never stage or commit them. Declare HEAD as fix and leave a clean tracked tree.

Reviewers never modify source or commit, including their output-only reports. Review against the entire original brief and acceptance criteria. Request CHANGES_REQUESTED only for a defect in the diff or an unmet acceptance criterion of the original brief. Record anything else in a FOLLOW-UPS section of artifacts/review.md; it does not affect the verdict. First reproduce suspected defects with a focused test or command, then run `make test-affected BASE=<original-base>` where the repository has that make target, using the pinned base recorded in the original brief; with Huyang, use `verify_run` with `test_scope=affected`. Otherwise run focused checks of the changed packages and their importers. Do not rerun the full declared gate: the producing fix task only succeeds after the worker has run its declared verification on the fix commit, and the final worker gate runs once where declared. artifacts/review.md starts with exactly VERDICT: ACCEPT or VERDICT: CHANGES_REQUESTED. Write artifacts/verdict.json as {"verdict":"accept","blocking_findings":0,"finding_titles":[]} or {"verdict":"changes-requested","blocking_findings":N,"finding_titles":["title"]}; keep both outputs consistent.

No-op rule: a fixer receiving an accept verdict checks out the preceding fix commit unchanged and declares that commit as fix. Keep exactly the preceding commit; create no report commit. Write untracked artifacts/handoff.md and artifacts/verification.log as "no-op: preceding review accepted <commit>". A final reviewer of a no-op carries the preceding accept only after checking the worker gate result, when a gate is declared. A failed gate must not be carried as acceptance.

Never submit nested campaigns, tasks or reviews. Do not claim acceptance as a fixer.
